-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",467,{
[14913]="700744F2\n1\tDestroy siege materials (total: 8)\tMaterials to construct siege engines moved into position to the east of Mizâdi's camp in the central area of the Hatokáli Fells. These engines cannot be allowed to become functional.\n2\tFind Mizâdi's scout\tWith the siege destroyed the encampment is safe. Find the scout and return to Mizâdi's encampment.\n",
[14914]="700744F4\n1\tDefeat Hatokáli sharp-shooters (total: 3)\030Defeat Hatokáli brutes (total: 6)\030Destroy the bandit barricades (total: 5)\tHatokáli bandits prepare to leave their encampment to journey northward, likely to bolster the ranks of the Ordâkhai warriors in the north. You must stop their advance.\n2\tConfront the Hatokáliri overseer\tYou destroyed the barricades built by the bandits, and assailed their position. Confront the overseer.\n3\tSpeak with the bandit overseer\tThe overseer, knowing he is defeated, begs you to stop and listen to him.\n4\tCollect the stolen treasure from the camp\tThe bandit overseer said that the treasure was not worth dying for and asked that you retrieve the price paid from within his camp.\n5\tFind Mizâdi's scout along the road to the north\tYou have the treasure and information that needs to be given to Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp.\n",
[14915]="700744F6\n1\tDefeat Ródruho Dôlo\tRetribution is at hand, as the location and name of a leader emerges. His crimes are brutal and innumerable and there is only one fitting punishment.\n2\tFind Mizâdi's scout\tThe menace of Ródruho Dôlo is ended. You should return to the entrance and speak with the scout.\n",
[14916]="700744F8\n1\tFree the captive labourers (total: 10)\tMizâdi's scouts will not leave the people of Mûr Ghala to suffer at the hands of the Utûgi or Ordâkhai. They have asked you to return and free the workers from their plight.\n2\tFind Mizâdi's scout\tYou freed a large number of builders and workers. They will take refuge with Mizâdi. You should find Mizâdi's scout and return to the encampment.\n",
[14917]="700744FB\n1\tRescue the builders from their fate (total: 10)\tMizâdi's scouts suggested that groups of builders and labourers are held against their will in the fortress to the south-east of Mizâdi's camp. They need to be freed. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tReturn to where you entered and speak with the scout\tThe workers are freed. Return to where you began and find the scout.\n",
[14918]="700744FC\n1\tDefeat the deserters (total: 16)\030Destroy the makeshift Ordâkhai camp (total: 8)\tThe bandits never intended to join the full Ordâkhai forces to the north. They were paid great sums of stolen riches to protect the escape of many Ordâkhai deserters. Your efforts thwarted the escape of many, and those left behind can now face justice.\n2\tFind Mizâdi's scout\tThe deserters are defeated and the remnants of their encampment are destroyed. Find Mizâdi's scout to return to the encampment.\n",
[14919]="70074500\n1\tDefeat Ordâkhai bóra (total: 8)\tReturn to the Ordâkhai fortress and eliminate the overseers who inflicted pain and suffering on the builders you rescued from captivity.\n2\tFind Mizâdi's scout\tThe bóra are eliminated. They can no longer harm the workers. You should return to the scout and then to Mizâdi's encampment.\n",
[14920]="70074505\n1\tComplete the mission: Investigative Efforts of the Hatokáliri\tMizâdi's scouts were discovered, but not before they saw the Utûgi and Ordâkhai head west off the south road from Emax Dûl. You have been asked to finish the work they would have done.\n2\tComplete the mission: Drive the Enemy Away\tYou reported back that the wood was treated to withstand the rigors of waves and water, and the tools are meant for a shipwright's hands. The scouts are planning to cause a distraction to draw the Utûgi and Ordâkhai away from the captives.\n3\tComplete the mission: Workers Released\tMizâdi's scouts were not able to free the labourers before the Utûgi returned. Kusâg asked that you return to the site and release the workers.\n4\tSpeak with Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp\tYou defeated the enemy and rescued their captives. You should return to Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp to ensure that all you rescued are safe and counted.\n",
[14921]="70074506\n1\tComplete the mission: The Scorpion Sting\tKhómabekh Dólo is making his final approach to the overrun village. You have been asked to face him, defeat him, and put an end to the threat he poses.\n2\tSpeak with Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp\tAfter defeating Khómabekh Dólo, Mizâdi's scout to the south arrived. They asked that you make your way back to speak with Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp.\n",
[14922]="70074507\n1\tComplete the mission: Deny Their Escape\tAfter being rescued, the labourers explained they built a few boats, and the enemy is using them to ferry their numbers in retreat across the river and into the jungle. This presents an opportunity to strand the enemy and visit righteous judgement on them.\n2\tComplete the mission: The Final Assault\tThe boats burn on the riverside, and the scout who retrieved you suggested they found the remaining camp of Ordâkhai and Utûgi on the north side of the river. Kusâg sent you to finish off the stragglers.\n3\tSpeak with Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp\tThe enemy has been defeated and the scout advised that you return to Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp.\n",
[14923]="70074508\n1\tComplete the mission: Inexorable Efforts\tMizâdi's scouts tracked the movements of the Ordâkhai of the crag overnight as they descended to the cross-roads south of Emax Dûl. A small force was left behind to defend cages and crates. With some clever activity, you may be able to sabotage these materials.\n2\tComplete the mission: Handling the Handlers\tYour success at sabotaging the containers to store and transport the scorpions may be for naught. Mizâdi's scouts report movement from the crag brings cat-handlers making their way to the cross-roads. By some means, these handlers and their cats can herd and control the scorpions. They must be stopped.\n3\tComplete the mission: The Who, What, and Why\tDespite your efforts, the Ordâkhai are still driven to recover the scorpions from the overrun village. A new set of orders, delivered whilst you were dealing with the cat-handlers, must be recovered to learn what the Ordâkhai intend, who leads them, and why their resolve is so strong.\n4\tSpeak with Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp\tAfter delivering the orders you recovered to the scout, you were directed to return to Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp and speak with her.\n",
[14924]="70074509\n1\tComplete the quest: Harvester's Flight\tAnother opportunity to do right by those oppressed by the hand of the Ordâkhai arises. Far to the east, where the river grows rapid and the bridge that crossed that river is crumbled, Ordâkhai overseers drive captive workers to harvest wood for the machine of war.\n2\tSpeak with Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp\tYou have defeated the overseers and rescued the labourers who toiled in the shadow of the fallen bridge. Return to Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp.\n",
[14925]="7007450A\n1\tComplete the mission: Before the Bombardment Begins\tOrdâkhai in the south-east continue to forge an offensive against Mizâdi's forces. A bold effort by the Ordâkhai endangers the camp as siege machinery is being prepared on the rocky outcroppings to the south-east of Mizâdi's camp. You have been asked to assist.\n2\tComplete the mission: A Harsh Punishment\tWith the materials to craft the weapons destroyed, Kusâg is told that more citizens of Mûr Ghala are captive within the fortress to the south-east. You are asked to intervene.\n3\tComplete the mission: End the Oversight\tYou freed the captive builders and saved them from a horrific fate. You discovered, however, a chain of overseers; cruel men who would visit terrible harm upon the captives. The scouts wish justice for those harmed by these wretches.\n4\tSpeak with Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp\tThe overseers are removed. Return to Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp.\n",
[14926]="7007450B\n1\tComplete the mission: Stop the Hatokáli Bandit Advance\tAt the bandit camp at the terminus of the road south of Emax Dûl, the bandits appear to be gathering in force. This can only mean an alliance is being considered between the bandits and the Ordâkhai. It must be severed quickly.\n2\tComplete the mission: A Harsh Truth\tAmong the bandits you discovered riches and wealth given to them by Ordâkhai deserters, paying for passage across the makeshift ferry at the bandit camp. Your action foiled the plot, and recovered the stolen wealth, but the Ordâkhai deserters still remain.\n3\tSpeak with Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp\tYou defeated the last of the Ordâkhai deserters. You should return to Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp to alert her to your victory.\n",
[14927]="7007450C\n1\tComplete the quest: Ending the Siege-lord\tWithin the walls of the fortress to the south-east, a threat looms. The siege-leader who means to build the machines of war to launch an assault against Mizâdi's mountain camp. You have an opportunity to bring an end to this campaign.\n2\tSpeak with Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp\tThough the battle was fraught, you were victorious over the siege-lord. Return to Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp.\n",
[14928]="7007450D\n1\tComplete the mission: Emissaries from the Ordâkhai\tScouts have tracked messages being exchanged between the Ordâkhai from the crags west of Mizâdi's camp and the Hatokáli bandits encamped on the river's edge at the terminus of the south road from Emax Dûl. Mizâdi's forces cannot afford these forces allying with one another.\n2\tSpeak with Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp\tThough you did all you could, it appears that emissaries have previously made contact with the Hatokáli bandits. Return to Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp to determine further action.\n",
[14929]="7007461E\n1\tSpeak with Mizâdi in Hanamíku\tSpeak with Shâra Mizâdi in Hanamíku. Hanamíku can be found in Pahar Hatokáli, which is south of Idagâl, within Mûr Ghala.\n",
[14930]="70074653\n1\tSpeak with Gíshu in Hanamíku\030Speak with Zâgsha in Hanamíku\030Speak with Nushâba in Hanamíku\tSpeak with each of the Subuzûri witnesses Shâra Mizâdi mentioned in Hanamíku.\n2\tGather some skins of fresh water for Gishu (total: 3)\030Gather new bandages for Zâgsha\030Find whetstones for Nushâba (total: 2)\tCollect each of the items for which Gíshu, Zâgsha, and Nushâba asked. Each can likely be found somewhere in or near Hanamíku in Pahar Hatokáli.\n3\tSpeak with Gíshu in Hanamíku\030Speak with Zâgsha in Hanamíku\030Speak with Nushâba in Hanamíku\tSpeak once more with the Subuzûri warriors Gíshu, Zâgsha, and Nushâba in Hanamíku.\n4\tSpeak with Shâra Mizâdi in Hanamíku\tSpeak with Shâra Mizâdi in Hanamíku. Hanamíku can be found in Pahar Hatokáli, within Mûr Ghala.\n",
[14931]="70074654\n1\tSpeak with the merchant Shâgigal Held-silver about his grievances\tSpeak with the merchant Shâgigal Held-silver about his grievances with Mizâdi's army. Shâgigal can be found within Hanamíku near the market stalls.\n2\tCollect oranges in Kirzâmur (total: 8)\030Collect deadfall wood in Kirzâmur (total: 10)\tCollect oranges and wood from deadfall to rebuild Shagigal's stalls and provide him with new fruit stock. The farmland of Kirzâmur should have some of both, south of Hanamíku.\n3\tBuild new market stalls for Shâgigal in Hanamíku (quantity: see journal)\tBuild new market stalls for Shâgigal in Hanamíku.\n4\tDestroy Shâgigal's burnt market stalls in Hanamíku (total: 3)\tDestroy Shâgigal's burnt market stalls in Hanamíku.\n5\tSpeak with Shâgigal Held-silver in Hanamíku\tSpeak with Shâgigal Held-silver now that the market stalls have been rebuilt and his fruit stock resupplied.\n6\tSpeak with Shâra Mizâdi in Hanamíku\tSpeak with Shâra Mizâdi in Hanamíku. Hanamíku can be found in Pahar Hatokáli, within Mûr Ghala.\n",
[14932]="70074656\n1\tNumûru told you to enjoy the party! Sample the various unique dishes within the party.\t\n2\tSpeak with Numûru upstairs at the party\tYou hear Numûru calling you from upstairs - perhaps you should find him?\n3\tSpeak with Numûru upstairs at the party\tNumûru looks like he would like to speak with you.\n4\tGuard the door for Numûru as he speaks with Mizâdi\tGuard the door for Numûru as he speaks with Mizâdi.\n5\tGuard the door for Numûru as he speaks with Mizâdi\tGuard the door for Numûru as he speaks with Mizâdi.\n6\tYou see an over-eager party-goer coming. Turn them away!\tYou see an over-eager party-goer coming this way. Turn them away!\n7\tGuard the door for Numûru as he speaks with Mizâdi\tGuard the door for Numûru as he speaks with Mizâdi.\n8\tGuard the door for Numûru as he speaks with Mizâdi\tGuard the door for Numûru as he speaks with Mizâdi.\n9\tYou see an over-eager party-goer coming. Turn them away!\tYou see an over-eager party-goer coming this way. Turn them away!\n10\tGuard the door for Numûru as he speaks with Mizâdi\tGuard the door for Numûru as he speaks with Mizâdi.\n11\tGuard the door for Numûru as he speaks with Mizâdi\tGuard the door for Numûru as he speaks with Mizâdi.\n",
[14933]="70074657\n1\tSpeak with Razâl in Ingarûma\tSpeak with Razâl in Ingarûma. Ingarûma is located on a large hill south of Hanamíku in Pahar Hatokáli.\n2\tSpeak with Razâl near the secret passage outside Imizíla\tSpeak with Razâl near the secret passage outside Imizíla. The secret passage can be found on the western side of Imizíla. Imizíla can be found south of Ingarûma.\n3\tMeet with the trader Katâl near Imizíla\tMeet with the trader Katâl by the secret gate into Imizíla.\n4\tFlee deeper into the secret channel beneath Imizíla\tFlee deeper into the secret channel beneath Imizíla.\n5\tPick up the key shining in the dirt\tPick up the key shining in the dirt in the channel.\n6\tSpeak with Razâl near Imizíla\tSpeak with Razâl near Imizíla.\n7\tSpeak with Razâl near Imizíla\tSpeak with Razâl near Imizíla.\n8\tSpeak with Shâra Mizâdi in Ingarûma\tSpeak with Shâra Mizâdi in Ingarûma. Ingarûma is located south of Hanamíku, high on a hill-top overlooking Imizíla.\n",
[14934]="70074658\n1\tSpeak with Numûru in Hanamíku\tSpeak with Numûru in Hanamíku about gathering supplies and food for the flagging Subuzûri.\n2\tSpeak with Quartermaster Lumgâna in Hanamíku\tSpeak with Lumgâna, the Hamâti quartermaster in Hanamíku.\n3\tHead to the abandoned town of Mûl Erebu\tHead to the abandoned town of Mûl Erebu, now overtaken by dangerous beasts. Mûl Erebu is located south of Hanamíku.\n4\tGather sacks of grain (total: 8)\030Gather kegs of wine (total: 6)\tGather sacks of grain and kegs of wine from the ruins of Mûl Erebu.\n5\tSpeak with Quartermaster Lumgâna in Hanamíku\tReturn and speak once more with Lumgâna, the Hamâti quartermaster in Hanamíku.\n6\tSpeak with Numûru in Hanamíku\tSpeak with Numûru in Hanamíku. Hanamíku can be found in Pahar Hatokáli, within Mûr Ghala.\n",
[14935]="70074659\n1\tJoin the conversation with Mizâdi and Numûru\tJoin the conversation with Mizâdi and Numûru.\n2\tJoin the conversation with Mizâdi and Numûru\tJoin the conversation with Mizâdi and Numûru.\n3\tSpeak with Mizâdi near Imizíla\tSpeak with Mizâdi near Imizíla.\n4\tDefend Mizâdi from the Ordâkhai counter-attack\tDefend Mizâdi from the Ordâkhai counter-attack!\n5\tDefend Mizâdi from the Ordâkhai counter-attack\tDefend Mizâdi from the Ordâkhai counter-attack! This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n6\tJoin Mizâdi and Numûru near the main gate of Imizíla\tJoin Mizâdi and Numûru once more near the main gate of Imizíla.\n7\tJoin Mizâdi and Numûru near the main gate of Imizíla\tJoin Mizâdi and Numûru once more near the main gate of Imizíla.\n8\tTake the main gate with Numûru\tJoin Numûru and the Subuzûri to take the main gate.\n9\tSpeak with Mizâdi to determine what to do next\tSpeak with Mizâdi to determine what to do next.\n",
[14936]="7007465A\n1\tArrive at the entrance to the secret passage into Imizíla\tArrive at the entrance to the secret passage into Imizíla. The secret passage can be found on the western side of Imizíla. Imizíla can be found south of Ingarûma.\n2\tMove through the secret passage past the gate into Imizíla\tMove through the secret passage past the gate into Imizíla.\n3\tSpeak with Razâl within Imizíla\tSpeak with Razâl beyond the secret passage gate into Imizíla.\n4\tDefeat Ordâkhai within Imizíla (total: 12)\030Set alight kegs of black powder (total: 8)\030Set alight batches of hot tar (total: 6)\tSet alight hot tar and kegs of black powder within Imizíla to create a distraction so Mizâdi and Rahâzi can slip into the city near Bârshud's fortress.\n5\tSpeak with Mizâdi outside Bârshud's fortress in Imizíla\tMove to and speak with Mizâdi outside Bârshud's fortress in Imizíla.\n",
[14937]="7007465B\n1\tSpeak with Razâl in Ingarûma\tSpeak with Razâl in Ingarûma. Ingarûma is located on a large hill south of Hanamíku in Pahar Hatokáli.\n2\tEnter Nakársong in the hills south-west of Ingarûma\tEnter Nakársong and free the captive lions and defeat their Ordâkhai trainers. Nakársong can be found south-west of Ingarûma in Pahar Hatokáli.\n3\tDefeat Ordâkhai trainers (total: 6)\030Destroy Ordâkhai lion cages (total: 7)\030Open lion paddock gates (total: 2)\tGo to Nakársong and free the captive lions and defeat their Ordâkhai trainers. Nakársong can be found south-west of Ingarûma in Pahar Hatokáli.\n4\tSpeak with Shâra Mizâdi in Ingarûma\tSpeak with Shâra Mizâdi in Ingarûma. Ingarûma is located south of Hanamíku, high on a hill-top overlooking Imizíla.\n",
[14938]="7007465C\n1\tSpeak with Razâl in Hanamíku\tSpeak with Razâl, Mizâdi's spy-master in Hanamíku.\n2\tSearch for a cluster of bootprints near Hanamíku\tSearch for clusters of bootprints near Hanamíku, showing the presence of Ordâkhai in the area.\n3\tSearch for clusters of bootprints further from Hanamíku\tSearch for clusters of bootprints further from Hanamíku, showing the presence of Ordâkhai in the area.\n4\tSearch for clusters of bootprints far from Hanamíku\tSearch for clusters of bootprints far from Hanamíku, showing the presence of Ordâkhai in the area.\n5\tScout just inside the camp\030Scout into the camp on the right to look for Ordâkhai bóra\tScout just inside the Ordâkhai camp to determine the number of Ordâkhai in the area, and any of their leaders.\n6\tSpeak with Razâl in Hanamíku\tSpeak with Mizâdi's spy-master in Hanamíku, Razâl. Hanamíku can be found in Pahar Hatokáli, within Mûr Ghala.\n",
[14939]="7007465D\n1\tSpeak with Ishumâni, the skilled woodworker within Hanamíku\tSpeak with Ishumâni, the skilled woodworker within Hanamíku.\n2\tGather cords of wood (total: 8)\030Gather young saplings (total: 6)\tGather cords of wood and young saplings to replenish the woodworker Ishumâni's stock of wood. Fresh wood can be found near Kirzâmur, south of Hanamíku.\n3\tSpeak with Ishumâni within Hanamíku\tReturn to Ishumâni, the skilled woodworker within Hanamíku with your freshly gathered supplies.\n4\tBuild wooden supports in Hanamíku (total: 4)\030Build a dance stage in Hanamíku\tHelp construct the new wooden supports and dance stage within Hanamíku.\n5\tSpeak with Numûru in Hanamíku\tSpeak with Numûru in Hanamíku. Hanamíku can be found in Pahar Hatokáli, within Mûr Ghala.\n",
[14940]="7007465E\n1\tSpeak with Shâra Mizâdi in Hanamíku when you are ready\tSpeak with Shâra Mizâdi in Hanamíku when you are ready.\n2\tSpeak with Shâra Mizâdi in Hanamíku\tSpeak with Shâra Mizâdi in Hanamíku.\n",
[14941]="7007465F\n1\tGather flowers south of Hanamíku (total: 6)\tGather flowers matching Numûru's description from the countryside south of Hanamíku.\n2\tSpeak with the jeweller Kutímu in Hanamíku\tSpeak with the jeweller Kutímu about fashioning a necklace from the stone Numûru gave you. Kutímu can be found within Hanamíku.\n3\tPick up drying fish near Kutímu's house (total: 4)\tPick up drying fish to feed to cats outside of Kutímu's house. Kutímu's house can be found south of Hanamíku, near Kirzâmur.\n4\tFeed Kutímu's cats outside of his house (total: 8)\tFeed Kutímu's cats outside of his house near Kirzâmur.\n5\tSpeak with the jeweller Kutímu in Hanamíku\tSpeak once more with the jeweller Kutímu now that all his cats have been fed. Kutímu can be found within Hanamíku.\n6\tSpeak with Numûru in Hanamíku\tSpeak with Numûru in Hanamíku. Hanamíku can be found in Pahar Hatokáli, within Mûr Ghala.\n",
[14942]="70074660\n1\tSpeak with the blacksmith Tebíra in Ingarûma\tSpeak with the blacksmith Tebíra in Mizâdi's camp at Ingarûma. Ingarûma can be found south of Hanamíku.\n2\tGather blacksmithing ore north of Ingarûma (total: 10)\tGather ore in the area north of Ingarûma for the blacksmith Tebíra.\n3\tRepair Subuzûri shields (total: 4)\tHelp the blacksmith Tebíra repair divots in Subuzûri shields in Ingarûma.\n4\tSpeak with the blacksmith Tebíra in Ingarûma\tSpeak with the blacksmith Tebíra in Ingarûma.\n5\tHelp the Subuzûri construct siege weapons (total: 3)\tHelp the Subuzûri in Ingarûma construct siege weapons to besiege Imizíla.\n6\tHelp the Subuzûri construct siege ladders (total: 4)\tHelp the Subuzûri in Ingarûma construct siege ladders to besiege Imizíla.\n7\tSpeak with Shâra Mizâdi in Ingarûma\tSpeak with Shâra Mizâdi in Ingarûma. Ingarûma is located south of Hanamíku, high on a hill-top overlooking Imizíla.\n",
[14943]="70074661\n1\tDefeat Hatokáli intimidators (total: 6)\030Defeat Hatokáli trackers (total: 4)\030Defeat Hatokáli skulkers (total: 2)\tDefeat Orcs within Roz Káskrauz. Roz Káskrauz is located in the hills east of Ingarûma.\n2\tDefeat Rogtúrz Night-eye in Roz Káskrauz\tDefeat Rogtúrz Night-eye within Roz Káskrauz. Roz Káskrauz is located east of Ingarûma.\n3\tSpeak with Shâra Mizâdi in Ingarûma\tSpeak with Shâra Mizâdi in Ingarûma. Ingarûma is located south of Hanamíku, high on a hill-top overlooking Imizíla.\n",
[14944]="70074662\n1\tEnter the valley below Ingarûma, near Imizíla\tEnter the valley below Ingarûma, near Imizíla.\n2\tDefeat Ordâkhai (total: 14)\030Aid wounded Subuzûri south of Ingarûma (total: 5)\tContinue moving south, defeating Ordâkhai and aiding wounded Subuzûri as you find them in the valley between Imizíla and Ingarûma.\n3\tDefeat Dhókhur Bóro in the valley\tDefeat Dhókhur Bóro in the valley below Imizíla.\n4\tPlace Mizâdi's banner to claim the valley for Hamât Renewed\tPlace Mizâdi's banner in the valley below Imizíla to claim it in the name of Hamât Renewed.\n5\tSpeak with Mizâdi outside the fort of Imizíla\tSpeak with Mizâdi outside the fort of Imizíla.\n",
})
